{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790264363,"nonce":"WDaCDOT6cVAf3VpuQZvigqt0x6o=","message":"THE ROOM LIBRARY, Dorian, 2026-09-24. Asked who draws the layouts: \"agent drafts, the wiki has each room type. If one proves too small we can always add a second. given the square or rectangular rooms (taking out a dividing wall) you can even rotate a full 360 or 180 degrees to make the layout feel more unique, ideally none should be desgined during the game though\"\n\n**Rulings, as he stated them**\n- **An agent drafts, and Dorian approves.** Every template stays marked draft until he approves it. Nothing unapproved reaches a game.\n- **One design per room type, at one size.** When a room proves too small in play, the answer is a second copy of it, not a bigger design.\n- **Rotation is how layouts get variety.** A square room is valid in all four rotations. A rectangle (two squares with the dividing wall taken out) is valid turned 180 degrees, and in both orientations on the grid.\n- **No layout is designed during a game.** The library is complete before play starts.\n\n**Room types.** These are the Core `RoomRoleDef`s on the bench (checked against its Defs, 2026-09-24):\n- Bedroom, Barracks, DiningRoom, RecRoom, Kitchen, Hospital, Laboratory, Workshop;\n- PrisonCell, PrisonBarracks, Storeroom, Tomb, Barn.\n\nThe library also covers two rooms that have no role of their own: the power room and the freezer. Classroom already exists and is re-cut.\n\nThe DLC room roles are not drafted: Nursery, Playroom, DeathrestChamber, WorshipRoom, ThroneRoom, CeremonialChamber, ContainmentCell. DESIGN's non-goals keep DLC colony management out of v1. INDEX lists them as deferred.","files":null}]}